h1 Manifest: an overview @17,49,694,25
h2 What it is @17,86,694,22
text Manifest is a way for an AI agent to put things on a screen and to see what is there, through one text tree. The agent writes MX, a compact one-node-per-line format; the engine lays it out, paints it, takes the user's input; and the agent reads the screen back as the same text, with the engine's own layout boxes and a short list of diagnostics, instead of a screenshot. @17,120,694,81
text Three decisions make it work: @17,213,694,20
text One vocabulary of roles with defaults. button "Export CSV" disabled is nine tokens and the renderer owns the look. Any node may take a position, a size and paint children, so the same tree can draw a funnel, a floor plan or a gauge down to the pixel, and every painted thing still carries a label and a role. Use the highest level that is faithful. @17,245,694,81
text Perception is the format. observe returns MX, so whatever the agent reads it can patch. Level 1 is the semantic tree; level 2 adds boxes; level 3 adds every shape. A query returns only what changed, as a patch. @17,338,694,61
text One engine. The core, the renderer, the host with lifecycle and input, and the MCP server are one Rust codebase that runs as a native window, headless, or as WebAssembly in the browser, with no browser dependency of its own. @17,411,694,61
h2 How it works @17,484,694,21
text agent ──MX──▶ engine ──pixels──▶ screen ▲ │ └──MX+boxes───┘ observe, look, events @17,517,694,21
text Parse: one line per node, IDs derived from labels, errors that name the line. @17,550,694,20
text Layout: flexbox and grid through taffy, text shaped from the bundled Inter font, sized nodes as coordinate spaces for positioned children, nested default looks for positioned nodes without paint. @17,582,694,40
text Paint: tiny-skia, at the screen's pixel density, light and dark palettes. @17,634,694,21
text Host: surfaces, revisions, lifecycle (ttl, seen, until, ephemeral, residues), pointer and key input that produce action and input events, tweens for nodes marked anim:. @17,667,694,40
text Perception: from the engine's own boxes, with !overflow, !overlap, !contrast, !tiny and !offcanvas. @17,719,694,21
text Transport: MCP over stdio, or the same calls from JavaScript against the wasm build. @17,752,694,20
h2 What it costs, measured @17,784,694,21
text All counts with Claude's tokenizer; reader accuracy with fresh Haiku readers that saw only the text. Full tables in . @17,817,694,41
link bench/results.md results.html @17,870,694,20
