h2 Where it sits @17,1191,694,21
text (Google) covers the write side: declarative components, no code, streaming. Manifest adds perception and lifecycle, and proposes both as A2UI v1.0 extensions with MX as an inference format; the compiler exists. @17,1224,694,61
text A2UI @17,1297,694,20
link docs/a2ui-extension.md a2ui-extension.html @17,1329,694,20
text MCP Apps and browser agents give models a UI or a page and a screenshot back. Manifest gives the tree back, and the engine is the only thing that paints it. @17,1361,694,41
text HTML paints everything but tells a model nothing about what it painted. The importer (import/) reads a rendered page and writes MX with semantics first and paint where nothing semantic fits. @17,1414,694,41
h2 Limits @17,1467,694,21
text Coordinates are expensive in any text format and models place things badly. The format's answer is defaults and layout owned by the engine; the loop's answer is observe level 2 and the !overlap and !offcanvas diagnostics. @17,1500,694,61
text Level 1 drops unlabelled shapes by design, so arrows that carry meaning need labels or a flow. @17,1573,694,20
text Buffers hold key:value numbers; each over records is not there yet. @17,1605,694,20
text The importer demotes a chart drawn with divs to paint; reading its values from an aria-label sentence is the next step. @17,1637,694,41
text No 3D, no keyframe animation, no plugin widgets. @17,1690,694,20
text Manifest is Apache-2.0. @17,1722,694,21
link "Source, issues and discussion on GitHub." https://github.com/brunopgalvao/manifest @17,1755,694,20
